Saund plunged to the ground.

193
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:48,000
While airshow catastrophes continued overseas,

194
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:51,680
America's flying circuses were struggling to stay aloft

195
00:13:51,681 --> 00:13:54,320
amidst strict new safety requirements.

196
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:59,960
Even after the 1926 Air Commerce Act,

197
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:01,160
airshows continued.

198
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:04,320
Airplanes, because of federal regulations,

199
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,920
were basically safer.

200
00:14:06,921 --> 00:14:07,621
U.S.

201
00:14:07,622 --> 00:14:17,020
aircraft regulation was also fueling a decade of innovation that made the 1930s the golden age of aviation.

202
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:26,980
Designers were attempting to make the airplanes more maneuverable, safer of course, to demonstrate for the general public.

203
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:34,820
Remember also that during the mid-30s to the late 30s, Europe was preparing for war.

204
00:14:34,821 --> 00:14:45,300
Many of the aircraft manufacturers at that time were building airplanes that could be used as military aircraft.

205
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:52,700
Renegade military pilots regularly displayed their new aircraft in unsanctioned military airshows,

206
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:57,840
often barnstorming under the guise of cross-country training missions.

207
00:14:57,841 --> 00:15:08,240
Between 1932 and 1936, the Army's flying trapezers performed 50 airshows for 50,000 people.

208
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:12,660
But the armed forces' disapproval of stunt flying continued,

209
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:16,240
until World War II took care of the problem for them.

210
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:23,140
World War II really caused the temporary succession of airshows

211
00:15:23,141 --> 00:15:26,040
because of shortage of airplanes, shortage of pilots.

212
00:15:26,041 --> 00:15:28,080
Everybody is dedicated to the war effort.

213
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:32,080
And after World War II, there were only, to my memory,

214
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:36,400
eight or ten pilots who were full-time devoted to air shows.

215
00:15:38,180 --> 00:15:41,320
Ironically, the war that had almost ended air shows

216
00:15:41,321 --> 00:15:45,640
now inspired a marketing strategy that would make them more popular than ever.

217
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:51,640
After the Second World War, Admiral Tester Nimitz decided that

218
00:15:51,641 --> 00:15:54,940
he wanted to form a team of naval aviators

219
00:15:54,941 --> 00:15:58,720
so that they could travel around the United States and help with the recruiting effort

220
00:15:58,721 --> 00:16:02,320
to get more young individuals in the Navy to be pilots.

221
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:08,980
With a single naval directive, air shows were transformed from entertaining family outings

222
00:16:08,981 --> 00:16:12,040
into targeted venues for military recruitment.

223
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:18,300
The very first flight leader, Lieutenant Commander Butch Voris, is the Blue Angels.

224
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:20,040
He is the one that designed the team.

225
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:22,240
They started in the summer of 1946.

226
00:16:22,241 --> 00:16:26,400
That year, they performed an air show in Omaha, Nebraska.

227
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:29,880
There were 300,000 spectators at that air show.

228
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:36,240
The instantly popular Naval Flight Exhibition Team was soon dubbed the Blue Angels.

229
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:40,560
The team flew rebuilt Grumman F6 F5 Hellcats.

230
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:46,340
Hellcats were piston-powered monoplanes, a sleeker product of the war, made of lightweight aluminum.

231
00:16:46,341 --> 00:16:47,041
them.

232
00:16:47,042 --> 00:16:53,140
The 1800 horsepower Hellcats were lightened further for stunts by removing their guns and

233
00:16:53,141 --> 00:16:58,734
ammo boxes from the wings and the oil tank armor from in front of the cockpit.

234
00:16:58,735 --> 00:16:59,435
They were

235
00:16:59,436 --> 00:17:03,020
then weighed down with 50 pounds in the tail to restore their center of gravity.

236
00:17:05,140 --> 00:17:10,800
Pretty quickly after the Hellcats, they switched to the Grumman Bearcat, which was a much hotter

237
00:17:10,801 --> 00:17:14,480
fighter airplane. It was the last of the great piston airplanes.

238
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:24,020
It was very popular for the air show for three or four years until the Blue Angels switched

239
00:17:24,021 --> 00:17:29,220
to another Grumman airplane, and that was the first jet that the Blue Angels used.

240
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:36,240
The Blue Angels' F9F Panther and Cougar jets forced the team to perform farther from the

241
00:17:36,241 --> 00:17:40,060
air show crowd than they had with their less powerful propeller-driven planes.

242
00:17:40,061 --> 00:17:47,680
The jets' engines also had to be modified to sustain longer inverted flight.

243
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:53,680
It was all done to further enhance the Blue's now famous formation flying.

244
00:17:56,140 --> 00:18:01,120
The Blue Angels started out originally flying with three airplanes in a V formation instead of a diamond

245
00:18:01,121 --> 00:18:04,880
because they had the enormous props in front of the World War II fighters that they used

246
00:18:04,881 --> 00:18:07,400
and they thought it was initially too dangerous to do that,

247
00:18:07,401 --> 00:18:11,440
But once they got into jets, they were solidified into the diamond-type formation that you see today,

248
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:13,520
and that's been the Blue Angel trademark ever since then.

249
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:22,920
Flown since 1947, the Blue Angel's diamond formation featured the flight leader, known as Boss, in position one.

250
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:28,340
Just below Boss and to the right was pilot number two, the right wing.

251
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:32,880
Below Boss on the left was pilot number three, the left wing.

252
00:18:32,881 --> 00:18:39,880
Pilot number four, known as the slot pilot, flew at the rear and bottom of the formation.

253
00:18:39,881 --> 00:18:46,880
By 1954, two solo pilots had been added to balance the airshow formation.

254
00:18:46,881 --> 00:18:50,880
The new six-plane configuration was called the Delta Formation.

255
00:18:50,881 --> 00:18:58,880
The Blues performed even their most intricate maneuvers only 18 to 24 inches apart from each other.

256
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:09,880
They maintain their precision formations at high speed by relying on markings called

257
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,880
paints, a system still used today.

258
00:19:12,881 --> 00:19:18,500
They'll take the wing tip or part of the wing and they'll line that up with maybe the R

259
00:19:18,501 --> 00:19:23,100
in Rob of my name and that's a certain formation that they fly for a particular maneuver and

260
00:19:23,101 --> 00:19:24,913
that's what they call their paint.

261
00:19:24,914 --> 00:19:28,060
And different maneuvers have what they call different paint

262
00:19:28,061 --> 00:19:29,060
settings.

263
00:19:29,061 --> 00:19:35,060
The Blue Angels' success inspired air forces around the world to follow suit in the 1950s.

264
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:38,120
From China's Thunder Tigers,

265
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:42,360
to the Italian Red Devils,

266
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:46,760
to the Netherlands Royal Air Force,

267
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:54,260
military jet teams were reigniting international enthusiasm for air shows.

268
00:19:54,261 --> 00:20:02,680
The post-World War II period gave birth to a number of aerial demonstration teams.

269
00:20:02,681 --> 00:20:10,620
In fact, most sovereign nations with any air aviation activities had some kind of demonstration team.

270
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:17,440
In 1953, the United States Air Force launched the Thunderbirds.

271
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:24,100
The team flew the Republic F-84G Thunderjets in 50 airshows during their first season.

272
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:33,420
In 1954, the team added a soloist to the Diamond and modified their jets to include smoke tanks for the first time.

273
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:38,820
They debuted their revised air show in Operation Will Tour,

274
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:46,280
traveling across 12 countries in South and Central America to perform before millions of dignitaries and spectators.

275
00:20:46,281 --> 00:20:55,720
the military teams around the world have done an enormous amount of good for air shows

276
00:20:55,721 --> 00:21:01,080
people will rally to the flag in whatever country it might be and generally speaking

277
00:21:01,081 --> 00:21:07,400
there will be larger attendance at an air show if you have a military flight demonstration team

278
00:21:07,401 --> 00:21:14,040
the thunderbirds and the blue angels soon began what would become decades of friendly rivalry

279
00:21:14,041 --> 00:21:16,360
Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen.

