military jet teams had reached

353
00:25:13,141 --> 00:25:15,140
new heights and speeds in their air show

354
00:25:15,141 --> 00:25:17,460
performances with the blue angels

355
00:25:17,461 --> 00:25:19,200
having beaten out the Thunderbirds

356
00:25:19,201 --> 00:25:21,600
to get to fly the massive and powerful

357
00:25:21,601 --> 00:25:23,400
new F4J Fanta

358
00:25:23,401 --> 00:25:27,900
but in their 1972-1973

359
00:25:27,901 --> 00:25:33,724
season, the Blues suffered injuries, the loss of aircraft.

360
00:25:33,725 --> 00:25:37,540
The first time, the remainder of their

361
00:25:37,541 --> 00:25:44,320
season was canceled, and the Phantom was replaced with the smaller and more economical A4F,

362
00:25:44,780 --> 00:25:48,940
a politically wise choice during the nation's worsening energy crisis.

363
00:25:50,460 --> 00:25:54,739
People remember lining up at gas stations to get their cars filled.

364
00:25:54,740 --> 00:25:56,400
Same was true of airplanes

365
00:25:56,401 --> 00:25:58,140
and fuel availability.

366
00:25:58,580 --> 00:26:00,680
So it had an impact on air shows.

367
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:05,720
In the 1980s, a rebounding economy and fuel supplies

368
00:26:05,721 --> 00:26:08,220
helped air shows make a strong comeback.

369
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:10,300
In North America alone,

370
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:13,480
they expanded from fewer than 200 annual events

371
00:26:13,481 --> 00:26:15,940
to over 300 near the end of the decade.

372
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:21,160
Then, on August 28, 1988,

373
00:26:21,960 --> 00:26:24,740
a collision ended the Italian jet team's performance

374
00:26:24,741 --> 00:26:27,960
at a U.S. Air Force air show in Rammstein, Germany.

375
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:31,540
One flaming plane spiraled into the stands,

376
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:34,880
killing 70 people and injuring nearly 400.

377
00:26:36,620 --> 00:26:40,280
International governments and citizens called for an end to air shows.

378
00:26:41,560 --> 00:26:43,340
But in the United States,

379
00:26:43,820 --> 00:26:46,700
strict Federal Aviation Administration safety standards

380
00:26:46,701 --> 00:26:48,420
kept air shows going strong.

381
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:53,760
Over the years, air show safety has been built on four fundamental premises.

382
00:26:53,761 --> 00:26:58,200
The first is that aircraft are never allowed to fly toward the audience,

383
00:26:58,400 --> 00:27:03,580
so that in the event of an accident, the plane would not continue into the audience and injure spectators.

384
00:27:04,020 --> 00:27:11,020
The second is that there's always a strict minimum distance kept between the airplanes performing aerobatics and the spectators.

385
00:27:11,680 --> 00:27:19,060
Thirdly, the FAA, in conjunction with our organization, runs a very strict pilot evaluation program

386
00:27:19,061 --> 00:27:23,100
to ensure the professional competence and piloting skills of the airshow pilots.

387
00:27:23,101 --> 00:27:28,220
And fourth, there's an imaginary cylinder that surrounds the air show area.

388
00:27:29,720 --> 00:27:37,260
Per FAA regulations, air show performers must perform their stunts within a restricted area called the aerobatic box.

389
00:27:38,040 --> 00:27:42,300
High-speed jets like those of the Blue Angels require the largest box,

390
00:27:42,740 --> 00:27:45,440
with a radius of 5 nautical miles from show center,

391
00:27:46,180 --> 00:27:49,220
a maximum flying altitude of 15,000 feet,

392
00:27:49,221 --> 00:27:54,040
and a minimum altitude of 500 feet over the spectator area.

393
00:27:56,660 --> 00:28:01,120
The aerobatic box's size varies by the speed and size of each aircraft,

394
00:28:01,520 --> 00:28:05,140
so all airshow performers must carefully rehearse their routines

395
00:28:05,141 --> 00:28:08,020
to remain inside of their box's dimensions.

396
00:28:09,900 --> 00:28:12,000
As a result of this prohibition,

397
00:28:12,180 --> 00:28:17,420
there's been not a single spectator fatality in the United States or Canada in nearly 50 years.

398
00:28:17,421 --> 00:28:22,580
That's a safety record, that's the envy of the entire motor sports industry

399
00:28:22,581 --> 00:28:28,040
and the kind of information that people need to know when they're thinking about getting up in the morning

400
00:28:28,041 --> 00:28:29,740
and attending their local air show.

