00:51:08,261 --> 00:51:10,100
more time to develop new products.

705
00:51:11,160 --> 00:51:18,060
Then in 1953, the rapidly expanding air show moved outside of Paris to its current home

706
00:51:18,061 --> 00:51:19,980
at Le Bourget Airfield.

707
00:51:23,040 --> 00:51:27,820
Great Britain's rival Farnborough Air Show has been open to the public since 1948.

708
00:51:29,300 --> 00:51:32,540
but Paris remains at the forefront of international airshows.

709
00:51:33,300 --> 00:51:37,860
The Paris Airshow is just monumental in size and scope.

710
00:51:38,280 --> 00:51:43,260
The exhibition area is about a million square feet of space,

711
00:51:43,500 --> 00:51:48,400
combining both the indoor space and the outdoor static display area.

712
00:51:48,820 --> 00:51:51,700
About 200 aircraft are on display.

713
00:51:52,440 --> 00:51:55,300
The exhibitors come from over 40 countries.

714
00:51:55,301 --> 00:51:59,380
the visitors come from practically every country on the planet.

715
00:52:00,900 --> 00:52:05,040
Look to your left now and you'll see Red 8 as he charges at over 500 miles per hour

716
00:52:05,041 --> 00:52:07,600
the good information approaching from your right.

717
00:52:08,300 --> 00:52:13,420
Today's international expos are a powerful combination of all that air shows have to offer.

718
00:52:14,460 --> 00:52:16,280
Top flight aerobatic entertainment,

719
00:52:17,280 --> 00:52:20,500
jet teams showcasing their military might,

720
00:52:20,501 --> 00:52:22,500
and roll!

721
00:52:22,501 --> 00:52:28,400
And the trade show's key focus, commerce.

722
00:52:29,700 --> 00:52:34,840
Families come, they picnic, they watch the flight, presentations that take place every afternoon.

723
00:52:34,841 --> 00:52:44,620
But the key thing, what makes this a world-class business event, is that from the Monday through the Friday, the show is open to professionals only.

724
00:52:44,621 --> 00:52:53,620
That's why companies flock to this show, to exhibit their products and services, because they're going to do business, big business.

725
00:52:55,120 --> 00:53:03,520
Familiar names from the golden age of the 30s are joined by modern powerhouses in private chalets bordering the Le Bourget runway.

726
00:53:05,380 --> 00:53:10,540
Alongside them are imposing national pavilions hosted by countries from around the world.

727
00:53:10,541 --> 00:53:15,360
where smaller private contractors display their aircraft.

728
00:53:18,180 --> 00:53:25,440
Throughout the day, ultra-modern aircraft perform public presentations and private sales demonstrations overhead.

729
00:53:29,200 --> 00:53:35,580
For eight days, foreign dignitaries and military representatives rub elbows with private buyers

730
00:53:35,581 --> 00:53:41,200
as the aviation industry offers the latest in airplane technology to the highest bidders.

731
00:53:42,680 --> 00:53:44,968
According to the estimates of the U.S.

732
00:53:44,969 --> 00:53:48,460
Department of Commerce at the last Paris Air Show in 1999,

733
00:53:49,240 --> 00:53:55,340
about $5 billion of business was signed for American companies alone.

734
00:53:55,860 --> 00:53:58,760
I think if you look at the global figure, the total participation,

735
00:53:59,520 --> 00:54:04,960
you're probably looking at about 10 times that figure in terms of the business that is signed on the dotted line.

736
00:54:05,580 --> 00:54:14,420
The high economic stakes at the Paris Air Show intensify pressure on the demonstration pilots as well.

737
00:54:15,760 --> 00:54:20,840
At the Paris Air Show, you want to gain attention for whatever company you're representing.

738
00:54:21,260 --> 00:54:26,620
So the excitement, the adrenaline is so high, I just can't even describe it to you

739
00:54:26,621 --> 00:54:30,920
because you've got the eyes of the world and the aviation world at least watching you.

740
00:54:30,921 --> 00:54:38,720
And each time I've flown, I say to myself, don't do anything dumb.

741
00:54:38,980 --> 00:54:42,720
I've seen a lot of accidents and fatalities at the Paris Air Show.

742
00:54:45,480 --> 00:54:50,600
In 1967, the air show's final performance was struck by disaster

743
00:54:50,601 --> 00:54:56,560
when one of the French national aerobatic team's jets crashed after it failed to pull out of a dive.

744
00:54:57,120 --> 00:55:00,180
The plane exploded into flames, killing the pilot.

745
00:55:00,920 --> 00:55:07,920
But the same extensive media coverage that broadcast the narrow miss of the crowd

746
00:55:07,921 --> 00:55:15,620
entices dozens of countries each year to bring their aircraft to international trade airshows.

747
00:55:18,080 --> 00:55:23,840
Airshows of this type are ideal venues to release or launch a new product.

748
00:55:24,400 --> 00:55:29,420
The Paris Airshow is attended by no less than 3,000 professional journalists.

749
00:55:29,421 --> 00:55:33,340
so you're going to have instantaneous coverage around the world.

750
00:55:35,020 --> 00:55:39,260
For the hundreds of thousands of visitors who actually attend these airshows,

751
00:55:39,780 --> 00:55:44,580
they're a rare opportunity to see and touch some of the world's most advanced aircraft.

752
00:55:46,200 --> 00:55:52,120
It is such moments the aviation community believes that ensure that these airshows will continue.

753
00:55:52,121 --> 00:56:01,460
Some people have thought that the virtual trade shows were going to make a dent in the

754
00:56:01,461 --> 00:56:03,460
trade show side of this.

755
00:56:03,461 --> 00:56:04,460
I don't think so.

756
00:56:04,461 --> 00:56:09,740
Nothing is ever going to take the place of actually being able to go and meet the company,

757
00:56:09,741 --> 00:56:15,680
the folks who manufacture the product, talk to them, shake hands, look at the product,

758
00:56:15,681 --> 00:56:17,180
feel it, touch it.

759
00:56:17,181 --> 00:56:19,400
Sometimes you can actually walk into it.

760
00:56:19,401 --> 00:56:21,360
So I think air shows are here to stay.

761
00:56:22,120 --> 00:56:32,220
Since early airshows introduced airplanes to the world and barnstormers brought aviation

762
00:56:32,221 --> 00:56:39,260
to the masses, airshows have sent military recruitment soaring, entertained millions

763
00:56:39,261 --> 00:56:46,280
of locals and tourists, and sold billions of dollars in aviation technology.

764
00:56:46,281 --> 00:56:48,640
Where will airshows go from here?

765
00:56:48,641 --> 00:56:50,720
The sky truly is the limit.

